## Command overview

```text
photon account
├── view
├── edit [--first-name <name>] [--last-name <name> | --clear-last-name]
│         [--idempotency-key <key>]
├── avatar
│   ├── upload <file> [--idempotency-key <key>]
│   └── reset [--yes] [--idempotency-key <key>]
├── 10dlc ...        # see 10DLC registration
├── oauth ...        # see OAuth connections
└── service-key ...  # see Service keys
```

## Profile

`account view` prints the account as Photon returns it:

```sh
photon account view --json
```

```json
{"accountId":"pho_acc_01k9yq3m7d2c8x4v6b5n0p1r2s","createdAt":"2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","deletedAt":null,"email":"user@example.com","firstName":"Ada","lastName":"Lovelace","phoneNumber":"+14155550123","phoneVerifiedAt":"2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z","pictureUrl":"https://...","updatedAt":"2026-07-03T00:00:00.000Z"}
```

<Note>
  `photon whoami` is the compact shortcut, with its own flat
  `{accountId, email, name}` contract. Use `account view` when you want the
  complete resource.
</Note>

`account edit` needs at least one name change. Names are trimmed, bounded, and
rejected when empty or when they contain control or format characters:

```sh
photon account edit --first-name Ada
photon account edit --last-name Lovelace
photon account edit --clear-last-name
```

The API has no way to clear a first name, so only `--clear-last-name` exists.

`account edit`, `account avatar upload` and `account avatar reset` print the
account Photon returns after the change, the same way `account view` does.

## Avatar

Upload accepts a regular JPEG, PNG, or WebP file up to 5 MiB, detected from the
file's signature rather than its extension:

```sh
photon account avatar upload ./avatar.webp
photon account avatar reset
photon account avatar reset --yes --json
```

The CLI requests a short-lived presigned form, uploads without a Photon
authorization header, and commits only once storage accepts the file. Presigned
URLs and form values are never printed.

`reset` prompts on an interactive terminal and needs `--yes` in scripts.
Declining prints `Cancelled.` on stderr and exits `1`.

Upload and reset are journaled. Before the commit step, an unresolved upload
keeps a private copy of the validated image so a replay does not need the
original file. See [Recoverable operations](/cli/operations).

<Note>
  Account deletion, phone verification, onboarding, account-level plans and
  invoices, 10DLC phone-number assignment, and messaging are deliberately
  outside this command surface.
</Note>
